+## Forgotten Archives reference pack (Player 2, 2026-10-14 playtest)
+- `forgotten-archives-gothic-style.png` — Cologne Cathedral at night: gothic verticality, dark stone, dramatic uplighting. The overall style target.
+- `archives-dark-corridor.png`, `archives-book-corridor.png` — shelf-lined corridors done right: shelves face the walkway, dense, aged.
+- `archives-old-reading-room.png` — decayed grandeur: peeling paint, worn floors, furniture with history.
+- `archives-warped-shelves.png` — what "unopened for centuries" looks like: warped wood, sagging shelves, decay.
+- `archives-dusty-study.png` — dust, debris, a chair no one has sat in for decades.
+- `archives-cobweb-skylight.png` — moonlight + cobwebs + scattered glowing books; the "abandoned magic" beat.
+- `archives-boss-arena-rotunda.png` — BOSS ARENA candidate: circular tiered rotunda, reads as a final exam.
+Direction notes: shelves must face like real bookshelves; textures need age (not flat concrete); add dust, broken furniture, decay/corrosion.
+
+## Hammer animation references (P2, 2026-10-14 playtest review)
+- `hammer-combo-3hit-10frame-ref.png` — THE left-click 3-hit combo, frame by frame: frames 1–5 = horizontal swings (hits 1–2, left/right with motion arcs), frames 6–10 = overhead raise into a planted slam with ground debris burst (3rd hit — the heavy finisher, NO jump per the redesign). This is the target for the combo redo.
+- `hammer-swings-8frame-ref.png` — general two-handed hammer swing reference: wind-up posture, full-body commitment, motion blur arcs. Note the grip and how the head stays parallel to the swing arc (ties to the head-orientation fix).
+
+- `hammer-leap-RMB-ref.png` — THE right-click mobility leap (hammer, melee only): crouch-launch, full arc with hammer raised overhead, landing with dust burst. Reference for the leap's trajectory feel and the raised-hammer pose mid-flight. Note: per the redesign the RMB leap is mobility (dash-plus: ~50% higher, a little further than a dash) — the landing impact here reads heavier than the spec, use for the arc/pose, tune the landing to match.
